  "summary": "Robert White won the D.C. delegate race, and advocates say the recent elections have created momentum for statehood efforts. Shadow Senator Ankit Jain is making a bid for D.C. Council, while the ACLU DC has highlighted key talking points about D.C. statehood for the public. D.C. and Virginia have sued the Trump administration over a proposed monument project. Without statehood, D.C. residents have no senators, and their one delegate to the House cannot vote on the House floor.",
